                <pb facs="0798" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00 Revolutions/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-24T16:00:00-04:40">February 24, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Your February 24, noon. Estrella Ureña, Tonio Jorge appear to be the leaders
                    of the revolution in Santiago but the nephew of the former, Jorge Estrella,
                    seems to be the commander. The National Army and its Commander in Chief are true
                    to the President.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
